<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document>
<name>Suggested stops</name>
<Style id="pin"><IconStyle><color>ff4C2700</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>https://www.gstatic.com/mapspro/images/stock/503-wht-blank_maps.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="line"><LineStyle><color>e64C2700</color><width>6</width></LineStyle></Style>
<Placemark><name>1 · Start: S Main &amp; E William</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.74845,42.27884,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2 · Main Street</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Downtown is the more grown-up part of Ann Arbor. I'd think of it as where you and Caitlin would come if Will ended up going here, or where you'd go if you wanted to take Will out somewhere nicer than a typical college-town restaurant.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.74855,42.282,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3 · Zingerman&#x27;s Deli</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The classic Ann Arbor deli. If College GameDay is ever in Ann Arbor, you'll see a shot of Zingerman's.<br><br>422 Detroit St]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.74515,42.2847,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4 · East Liberty Street</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The more student-feeling stretch of downtown.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.745,42.27958,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5 · Modern Languages Building</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A good example of a large lecture hall. This is the kind of classroom where Will might take an intro course like Intro to Psychology.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73909,42.27989,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6 · Burton Memorial Tower</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The classic college bell tower.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73871,42.27942,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7 · Michigan League (optional)</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Worth poking your head in if it's open, though I don't really know what the League does or is for.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73771,42.27935,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8 · Hill Auditorium</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Will will have his freshman welcome here. Peek your head in if it's open.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73908,42.27918,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9 · The Diag</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[This is the block M they'll show on College GameDay. You're not supposed to step on it until you've taken your first exam.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73801,42.2771,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>10 · Angell Hall &amp; the Fishbowl</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Take a look inside. For lack of a better term, it's the heart of LSA, or at least it's representative of the LSA experience.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73975,42.27672,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>11 · Shapiro Library &amp; Hatcher</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[If seeing a library is important to Will, check out Shapiro. It's called the UGLi. You can also check out Hatcher, which has the stacks, which I feel like is a quintessential college thing.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73719,42.27563,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>12 · Engineering Arch</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Leave the Diag through the arch under West Hall.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73627,42.27543,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>13 · East Quad</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[East Quad has a weird residential program. Unless Will has a very specific vision of never leaving his dorm his freshman year, I wouldn't recommend it.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73516,42.27293,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>14 · Ross School of Business</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The new Ross building, which didn't exist when I was there, is a much, much nicer version of the business school I went to. Note the name of the street.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.73697,42.27278,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>15 · Law Quad &amp; Law Library Reading Room</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Go look at the Law Library Reading Room if somebody will let you in. Tell Will he can pretend he's Harry Potter when he studies there.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.739,42.274,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>16 · Michigan Union</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[I don't really know what goes on in the Union, but they do have a bunch of food options in the basement.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.74151,42.27517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>17 · The Cube</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[For some unknown reason, this is a Michigan landmark. Go spin it around.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.74189,42.2759,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>18 · South State Street</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Walk down South State Street. It borders the campus, with bars and restaurants, and it'll give you a good feel for what it's like walking around the university. You can buy some swag at Rally House.<br><br>Rally House, 303 S State St]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.74064,42.27916,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>19 · Back downtown</name><styleUrl>#pin</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Frita Batidos is just past Main on W Washington if you're hungry.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-83.7479,42.2805,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
